{"duration": 62.723, "exact_word_timing": true, "lines": [{"beat": 0, "text": "Mendeleev arranged elements in columns, leaving gaps for elements nobody had found.", "start": 0.08, "end": 4.854}, {"beat": 0, "text": "In St. Petersburg in 1869, Mendeleev's table had empty spaces.", "start": 5.074, "end": 9.825}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Not every element had been found yet.", "start": 10.245, "end": 12.135}, {"beat": 1, "text": "Mendeleev left those spaces empty instead of hiding them.", "start": 12.355, "end": 15.504}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Mendeleev sorted elements by atomic mass, a measure of an atom's weight.", "start": 15.924, "end": 19.934}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Elements with similar chemical behavior went into the same column.", "start": 20.154, "end": 23.671}, {"beat": 2, "text": "In Mendeleev's table, the same properties kept returning, column after column.", "start": 23.891, "end": 28.402}, {"beat": 3, "text": "You see, it is like sorting socks by color, so a missing pair still tells you what to buy.", "start": 28.822, "end": 33.446}, {"beat": 4, "text": "The real reason was Mendeleev's law: chemical properties depend on atomic mass.", "start": 33.866, "end": 38.594}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Because properties repeated, Mendeleev's pattern pointed to what was missing.", "start": 38.814, "end": 42.664}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Mendeleev made bold predictions about elements nobody had found.", "start": 42.884, "end": 46.53}, {"beat": 5, "text": "The answer came later, with atomic numbers and quantum mechanics.", "start": 46.95, "end": 50.417}, {"beat": 5, "text": "By the late 1800s, Mendeleev's table was the one everyone accepted.", "start": 50.637, "end": 54.805}, {"beat": 5, "text": "Today, groups follow outer electrons, and 118 elements now fill the table Mendeleev left with gaps.", "start": 55.025, "end": 61.603}], "words": [{"w": "Mendeleev", "start": 0.149, "end": 0.674, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "arranged", "start": 0.724, "end": 1.149, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {